  {
   "id": "Rw-2HCzBcFIJ",
   "from": "Dennis Murphy",
   "author": "0c39e60ddb38622b",
   "date": "2015-05-31T05:12:23Z",
   "subject": "Re: Enforcing more logarithmic axis ticks under free scales in facet_wrap()",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">free_x certainly doesn&#39;t help you since it&#39;s clear the x-ranges among the facets are quite variable. All I could suggest would be to manually set breaks in scale_x_log10() so that you can guarantee a minimum of two tick marks per facet. Since we don&#39;t have that information available, you&#39;ll have to figure that out for yourself.<div><br></div><div>BTW, interesting graph - it looks like a poor man&#39;s density strip plot. I like it :)</div><div><br></div><div>Dennis</div></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Fri, May 29, 2015 at 10:20 PM, trichter <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">tric...@uni-bremen.de</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br></div></div>"
    ],
